// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the size of the list), then for every valid index before the specified index, either both the current and previous values at that index are null, or the current value at that index equals the previous value at that index.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every valid index up to the specified index, either both the current and previous values at that index are null, or the current value at that index remains unchanged from its previous value.
